<urn:atm:triage:finding/AG18-QA-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AG18-QA-003" ;
  triage:title "Send-vs-ack dispatch fork relocated, not deleted (repeatable ladder-wide pattern)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/dispatch_delivery.rs:58-72 (dispatch_send, renamed from dispatch_compose_send) still branches on request.acknowledges_message_id.is_some() && request.source_remote_host.is_none() into two separate downstream execution/finalization paths (ack_mail_with_runtime_... vs send_mail_with_runtime_...) producing AckOutcome vs SendOutcome. quality-mgr resolved the reviewer split (req-qa: open pending ruling; ruthless-boundary-qa: blocking) in favor of blocking -- the sprint doc's ack-as-data carve-out describes SendRequest construction, not license for a pre-routing boolean fork to two separate outcome-typed handler functions. Cited as an open ladder-wide finding (AG18-QA-003) already present across every sub-sprint branch s18-s25 -- full repeatable-pattern sweep executed across all 8 branches plus integration branch." ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA-003" ;
